    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>DogWash Perle & Co is a self-service dog washing and drying station on chemin des Plaines in Mouans-Sartoux, between Cannes and Grasse. The project, run by Baptiste Paladino, opened in early 2026 in the presence of local officials and received an interest-free loan of €8,000 via Initiative Terre d'Azur — two points reported by several regional outlets (France 3 Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, municipal communications) which confirm the place exists and where it is located.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The space offers three ways to wash your dog: self-service with tailored programmes (bath and dry, aloe vera shampoo, strawberry-scented conditioner), classic grooming by appointment, or a "dog taxi" service for owners who'd rather have their dog picked up. The station reportedly accepts dogs up to 80 kg. Advertised opening hours are 7 days a week from 9am to 7pm, but <strong>exact prices could not be found online</strong> — ask directly on site or via the business's social media before going.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: as the place is recent (opened in 2026), online reviews are still scarce — a call ahead lets you confirm self-service availability, especially during busy summer hours.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Mouans-Sartoux sits between Cannes, Grasse and Mougins, a handy area to combine this wash stop with a walk in the Grasse hinterland or a visit to the nearby Parc de la Valmasque.</p>
